  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Franklin College is a private liberal arts institution in the charming town of Franklin, Indiana. Founded in 1834, the college boasts a stunning 207-acre wooded campus, giving you a serene place for your studies. With around 1000 students, the college fosters a close-knit community.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>At Franklin College, you become part of a vibrant and inclusive campus community, among international students from 15 countries. The university provides many opportunities to enhance your student life. You can choose from various student organisations that interest you. Additionally, the university offers you mental support programs and personalised guidance to help with your well-being.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>At Franklin College, you can choose to live on campus in one of their four residence halls or three campus homes. Each of these offers you a variety of amenities, including air conditioning, Wi-Fi, and communal spaces.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><i>If you’re looking for budget-friendly accommodation options outside the campus, feel free to </i><a href=\"https://edvoy.com/app/\"><i>download our app</i></a><i> and check out the Stays feature!</i></p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<p><strong>Library</strong></p><p>The B.F. Hamilton Library at Franklin College offers you a wealth of resources and services. Plus, you can access the 24-hour computer lab at the library.</p><p><strong>Sports</strong></p><p>At Franklin College, you can be part of their sports teams competing in NCAA Division III. The college also has expansive fields for sports like football, soccer, and baseball, giving you plenty of choices for playing team sports or simply enjoying physical activity.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
